PHP 8.6 removed the INI_INT()/INI_STR() macros (replaced by
zend_ini_long_literal()/zend_ini_string_literal()), the XtOffsetOf() alias of
offsetof(), the EMPTY_SWITCH_DEFAULT_CASE(), WRONG_PARAM_COUNT and
ZEND_WRONG_PARAM_COUNT() macros and the zval_is_true() alias of zend_is_true()
(see UPGRADING.INTERNALS), and ext/hash's php_hash_bin2hex(), which
zend_bin2hex() replaces. phpredis renamed the call sites on its develop branch
in several commits: 78c1c690 "Fix PHP 8.6 builds" (INI_INT, INI_STR,
XtOffsetOf, EMPTY_SWITCH_DEFAULT_CASE), 7d4fa613 and 3401462e (the two
WRONG_PARAM_COUNT macros), 8e1c2789 (zval_is_true), e3273a90 and dd15a7dd
(php_hash_bin2hex). 78c1c690 and the two bin2hex commits change a
php_compat.h that 6.3.0 does not have, so they do not apply to 6.3.0. This
patch provides the eight names instead, with the definitions PHP 8.5 had (or
the replacement names UPGRADING.INTERNALS gives), for PHP >= 8.6 only, in the
header every source file includes. The zval_dtor() removal and the zend_string
session save_path are covered by the cherry-picked upstream commits d24528e1
and b8b765e6. Drop this patch and the two cherry-picks with the first release
that has all of these commits; there is none after 6.3.0 yet.

diff --git a/common.h b/common.h
index 8936c8e0..825b4d15 100644
--- a/common.h
+++ b/common.h
@@ -13,6 +13,18 @@
 #include <zend_smart_str.h>
 #include <zend_smart_string.h>
 
+/* PHP 8.6 removed these; spell them as the replacements UPGRADING.INTERNALS names. */
+#if PHP_VERSION_ID >= 80600
+#define INI_INT(name) zend_ini_long_literal(name)
+#define INI_STR(name) ((char *) zend_ini_string_literal(name))
+#define XtOffsetOf(s_type, field) offsetof(s_type, field)
+#define EMPTY_SWITCH_DEFAULT_CASE() default: ZEND_UNREACHABLE(); break;
+#define ZEND_WRONG_PARAM_COUNT() do { zend_wrong_param_count(); RETURN_THROWS(); } while (0)
+#define WRONG_PARAM_COUNT ZEND_WRONG_PARAM_COUNT()
+#define zval_is_true(op) zend_is_true(op)
+#define php_hash_bin2hex(out, in, in_len) zend_bin2hex((out), (in), (in_len))
+#endif
+
 #define PHPREDIS_GET_OBJECT(class_entry, o) (class_entry *)((char *)o - XtOffsetOf(class_entry, std))
 #define PHPREDIS_ZVAL_GET_OBJECT(class_entry, z) PHPREDIS_GET_OBJECT(class_entry, Z_OBJ_P(z))
 
